regcf-denovo.l4:1865:5-9:
  I found a problem while checking the definition of `the issuer's § 227.201 disclosure duty`:
    This LEST can never be reached, because the rule has no deadline.
    
    After MUST, the LEST is what follows when the deadline passes without the action.
    This rule has no WITHIN and no BEFORE, so it waits for its action however long it takes, and time alone never takes it to this LEST.
    
    To say by when the action is due, add a WITHIN (or a BEFORE). Otherwise, remove the LEST.
